# Copy this file to .env and fill it in to send real emails, then restart `npm start`.
# Without a .env the app runs in TEST MODE: emails are saved to ./outbox instead of being sent.

# ===== Microsoft 365 (recommended) — Microsoft Graph =====
# Your IT admin creates an app registration once (steps in README.md → "Microsoft 365 setup").
MS_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
MS_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
MS_CLIENT_SECRET=paste-the-client-secret-value-here
# The mailbox the cards are sent from (a shared mailbox works well, e.g. exams@cit.lk)
MS_SENDER=exams@yourdomain.lk
# Optional
# MAIL_FROM_NAME=CIT Examinations
# MAIL_REPLY_TO=exams@yourdomain.lk

# ===== Or: plain SMTP (only if SMTP AUTH is enabled for the mailbox) =====
# Leave the MS_ lines out to use this instead.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.office365.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=exams@yourdomain.lk
# SMTP_PASS=password
# MAIL_FROM="CIT Examinations <exams@yourdomain.lk>"

# ===== Other =====
# PORT=5173
# BROWSER_PATH=C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft\Edge\Application\msedge.exe
